WEBVTT

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:20.620
Where am I?

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.590
Why am I in the water?

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:28.670
What's that? A ball?

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:33.680
Huh? What is this? It makes no sense.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.020
Huh? What? What the--?!

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:52.660
...and you know what the teacher said?

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:56.910
"Kiyomizu won't know,
but let's hear her answer."

00:00:56.910 --> 00:01:01.330
Isn't that awful? I couldn't believe it!

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:08.420
Then again, I really didn't
know how to answer.

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:11.260
Whoops! I've gotta go shopping!

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:14.890
Onion sprouts are cheap today.

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:17.560
Well, see you tomorrow!

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:33.660
Doc! My brother! My brother--!

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:36.870
That day...

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:43.000
...I finally woke after 203 days of sleep.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:21.510
I'm told that I played water polo
for three years in junior high.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:27.560
I totally can't remember, but apparently,
I was an incredible player.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:32.190
We won a national tournament
in winter of my third year.

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:38.240
The Momotaro Cup even allowed high school
freshmen, so that's pretty sweet.

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:45.790
I guess my mom came to cheer me on,
but we got in a car crash heading home.

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:50.170
It was an awful accident
that left me in bad shape.

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:55.170
I was unconscious for half
a year plus three weeks.

00:03:55.170 --> 00:04:00.720
And when I finally woke up,
I'd lost three years of memories.

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:07.050
Episode 1:                Sorry, Who Are You?

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:07.890
I can't remember a single thing
about my life in junior high.

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:13.730
It's like I'm back in 6th grade,
so that's a weird feeling.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:17.780
My mom, dad, and Asumi look a bit older.

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:23.740
And Asumi's so big now! Her being
in junior high, she's like my elder!

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:24.910
Well?

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:26.120
Hmm?

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:28.580
Have you remembered anything?

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:30.830
Uh, not yet.

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:32.080
I see.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:37.010
Well, no rush. The doc said
we should be patient.

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:38.380
No worries!

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:40.220
Yup.

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:42.550
I don't need to remember.

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:45.850
I'm just glad to be alive.

00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:49.730
My memories don't matter as much.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.730
Excuse me!

00:04:49.730 --> 00:04:50.560
They're here!

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:52.060
Come in!

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:08.660
It's Minato!

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:10.330
U-Um...

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:13.580
S-Sorry! Did that hurt?

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:14.750
We're just so excited!

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:17.380
That's not it...

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:20.670
Sorry... Who are you?

00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:26.850
It's your water polo team
from junior high.

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:28.770
Oh...

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:32.020
Yeah?

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:34.520
That's very kind of you.

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:39.230
This is Advisor Bizen.

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:40.820
Hello.

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:42.450
It's been a while.

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:47.370
You really don't know who we are?!
After all we've been through?!

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:49.080
Relax, Momo.

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:51.830
We were "Shogaku's Elite Four"!

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.580
We won Nationals!

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:56.790
You've gotta remember that, right?!

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:59.840
I'm sorry.

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:12.470
4 Months Later

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:17.480
Hasn't changed much in three years.

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:21.690
Three years isn't that long of a time.

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:23.450
I guess.

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:35.120
I've changed more than anything. I'm 20 cm
taller and my face looks different.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:36.960
It's so weird.

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:45.510
After four months of rehab and stuff,
I finally returned to home sweet home.

00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:51.970
We live at my dad's shop, the terribly
named "Memory Shop Kiyomizu."

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:52.220
"Memory Shop Kiyomizu"
"Autumn Silver Week Sale!" "Shop Online!"

00:06:51.970 --> 00:07:00.480
It's a souvenir shop in Kurashiki Bikan
that mainly sells jeans, plus other junk.

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:02.190
I'm home.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:08.450
Well, this place hasn't
changed a whole lot.

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:11.740
Huh? What?! Kamekichi?!

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:12.540
Yup.

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:17.460
Wha--?! I remember him
being just this big!

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:19.920
Now he's the shop mascot.

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:24.300
Yeah? You've grown so much!

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:26.930
Huh?

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:32.430
Wait! Did that thing sell?!
Did someone actually buy it?!

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:36.850
Whoa! It's still here!

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:44.360
It's "art" I threw together in 4th grade
that I'd hoped someone might buy.

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:41.270
Masterpeace

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:41.270
yen

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:48.820
Of course it hasn't.
Nobody even looks at it.

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:54.580
That's bullshit. Tons of people
buy junk on vacation.

00:07:54.580 --> 00:07:57.120
You're still as dumb as ever.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:00.080
Hey! Hmm?

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:02.250
That's a relief.

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:07.760
Thank goodness.

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:11.260
I sure missed your comedy duo.

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:14.010
We're not a duo, Mom!

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:18.310
I'm sorry, Minato.

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:21.690
Whatever. I don't take offense.

00:08:21.690 --> 00:08:25.690
If I hadn't gotten in that accident,
you wouldn't have--

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:30.160
That's why you're sorry?
Let's drop the doom and gloom!

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:34.160
The Kiyomizu house is
a happy place! Cheer up!

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:36.080
Yeah!

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:39.750
It's okay! Everything will
go back to normal!

00:08:40.670 --> 00:08:42.170
Right!

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:49.130
Seeing my mom trying her best
to smile, I wanted to act cool.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:54.390
That settles it! To make things
normal again, I'll get back into it!

00:08:54.390 --> 00:08:56.810
I'll play water polo again!

00:08:56.810 --> 00:09:00.350
I'll be a champion in no time at all!

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:04.110
Having said that...

00:09:05.070 --> 00:09:10.950
This photo doesn't even feel real.
And what weird hats.

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:20.080
"Water Polo Rules Book"
"Water Polo Skills & Training"

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:23.250
I guess I really did play water polo.

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:26.330
"Water Polo Rules Book"

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:26.250
What's this old book?

00:09:27.090 --> 00:09:32.550
"Remain. One type of rule
violation in water polo.

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:38.390
Refers to receiving the ball within
two meters of the opponent's goal.

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:44.190
'Remain offsides' in the sense
of remaining near the goal."

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:47.610
I totally don't get it!

00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:58.240
Dude... Check out my body.

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:09.800
No way! I can't do it!

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:14.260
It's nuts how much muscle I lost
while sleeping half a year!

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:17.930
I'll just tell Mom, "Sorry!
No water polo for me!"

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:21.600
The sooner I tell her,
the less it'll hurt! Yup!

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:25.230
Could you help me pick out
a present for my dad?

00:10:25.230 --> 00:10:26.360
Of course.

00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:30.440
Just ask and we'll order it for you.

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:37.280
Ebisu Shopping Street
towards Ohara Museum of Art

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:37.280
Ebisu Shopping Street
towards Ohara Museum of Art

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:41.750
What to do... This sucks.

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:44.420
I shouldn't have said I'd play again.

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:46.330
"Mikoshiba Books"

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:49.670
Hmm?

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:52.000
"Featured in this month's <i>Swimming</i>!"
"Shogakukan Senior High School
Water Polo Club Interhigh Champs"

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:54.250
"Support our local team!"

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:16.030
"From 'Elite Four' to 'Three Musketeers'"

00:11:09.570 --> 00:11:16.320
"These three freshmen starters at the
prestigious Shogakukan High School

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:19.320
won Interhighs in their first year."

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:20.910
From 'Elite Four' to 'Three Musketeers'

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:20.910
These 'Three Musketeers' are Riku Momosaki,

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:20.910
Keita Kakihana, and Koki Toguchi.

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:25.120
We were "Shogaku's Elite Four"!

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:31.000
I give up. The difference in skill
is way too much-- Huh?

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:34.080
Chinu Kawakubo

00:11:34.050 --> 00:11:38.090
What a cutie! Chinu, huh?

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:46.890
Whoa! C-Can I help you?

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:52.110
Minato-<i>senpai</i>! I've been looking for you
since Asumi said you're back!

00:11:52.110 --> 00:11:54.650
Sorry, I don't remember you.

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:59.450
What? Even me?! It's Eitaro Oka!

00:11:59.450 --> 00:12:00.780
Uh, no?

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:05.160
The same guy you said
had rockin' glasses, Eitaro!

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:06.250
No?

00:12:06.250 --> 00:12:10.630
The guy who thought it was "taxicrab"
and made you laugh!

00:12:10.630 --> 00:12:12.250
Still no.

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:17.800
No way! You're the one who
showed me the joys of water polo!

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:20.220
You taught me the eggbeater!

00:12:20.220 --> 00:12:23.310
You've lost me.

00:12:23.310 --> 00:12:25.850
Which high school will you go to?

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:28.810
Hmm? High school?

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:34.110
Shogakukan has a high school to
advance to, but it's hard to get in.

00:12:34.110 --> 00:12:39.660
And since I heard you won't make
the cut, where will you go?

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:40.530
Hmm?

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:47.370
I wanna play water polo with you again,
so I'll go wherever you do!

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:51.330
Oh! Did my words just touch your heart?

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:53.920
I'll say it again! I wanna play--!

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:55.340
Oh, no!

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:55.960
Huh?

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:59.380
This is trouble! Shoot!

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:00.090
What?

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:03.140
I haven't been thinking about school!

00:13:03.140 --> 00:13:07.770
If I was in 9th grade,
that means I'll be in high school now!

00:13:07.770 --> 00:13:09.640
Oh, hell no!

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:13.060
Senpai! I'll follow you to
whatever high school--!

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:15.860
Sorry! I've got bigger problems!

